Hi Drea, here is the updated running order for the interview day. Please share the timings with the people who are coming so we can keep the room quiet while each interview is recorded.

We will arrive at eight to bring in the lighting and test the sound. The first interview can start at nine. Each slot includes a few minutes to settle in, check the microphone and explain where to look. There is a break after the second interview, then we will record the remaining two before lunch.

For the room, could you arrange:
- four ordinary chairs, without wheels if possible;
- a small table for water;
- a place to leave coats away from the camera;
- the display samples you want in the background.

We will film the demonstration after lunch, once the interview equipment is packed away. Please tell us if the sample needs time to warm up. We can use that interval to record the room details and any close shots of the controls.

Thanks,
Ellor

Tobin, thanks again for organising the food collection. We have room for the boxes in the side hall, so there is no need to carry them up the steps at the front. A volunteer will meet the van and show the driver where to unload.

Could you sort the donations into these broad groups before bringing them?
- tins and jars;
- pasta, rice and other dry goods;
- breakfast items;
- toiletries, kept in a separate box.

Please leave the original labels on everything. It helps our team check dates and put the right items together. If a box is especially heavy, split it between two smaller boxes rather than filling it to the top. We have a few empty cartons here if you run out. After unloading, you are welcome to stay for a cup of tea and see how the sorting tables work. Let me know roughly how many volunteers will be with you so we can have enough mugs out.

Nessa

Hi Galen, we look forward to seeing you on Friday. Check-in starts at two, but you can park in the day area earlier if you want to have lunch or walk the trail. Please stop at reception before taking your vehicle to the site.

A few useful things to bring:
- a torch for the path to the washrooms;
- a groundsheet if you have one;
- a long charging cable for the powered site;
- a bag for taking recycling to the collection point.

The small shop stocks milk, bread and ice, though it closes before reception. There is a drinking-water tap beside each pair of sites. Please use the washing-up area for dishes rather than the washroom basins. Quiet hours start at ten, and we ask everyone to keep music low even earlier in the evening. If you arrive in heavy rain, come into reception first and we will help you choose the driest place to pitch. The trail map is on the noticeboard and paper copies are available at the desk.

Safe travels,
Brisa

Hello Velin, I have noted that the dining table comes apart and that you will pack the kitchen yourself. Please keep the screws with the table in a labelled bag so they do not disappear into a general box.

For the last evening, it helps to keep one small box out for the kettle, mugs, chargers and anything you will need straight away. Label that box clearly and ask the crew to put it on last. Please empty and dry the washing machine before we arrive. We can carry it, but the appliance connections should already be disconnected.

On the day:
- leave a clear path from each room to the front door;
- point out anything that must stay in the property;
- tell the crew which boxes contain fragile items;
- check cupboards and high shelves before we leave.

You don't need to dismantle the bed if you would like the crew to do it. Just leave the mattress clear. We will check the room labels with you at the new place before unloading.

Best wishes,
Orsa

Alba, here are the practical details for sale day. Please use the marked unloading lane and wait for the yard team to wave the truck forward. They will check the lot description against the paperwork before moving the animals through.

Bring the following with you:
- the signed vendor declaration;
- a copy of the transport booking;
- the catalogue correction, if you still need it made;
- the contact name for whoever is taking the truck home.

The office opens before the first unloading slot. Tea and breakfast will be available from the canteen, and there is a seating area beside the ring. Please keep the pedestrian lane clear while trucks are moving. If you are bringing someone who has not been to the yards before, ask them to wait by the office until you can show them around.

We will announce any change to the order of sale over the speakers and write it on the board outside the office. Do not rely on an old printed programme if a change has been announced. Your catalogue wording now matches the description you confirmed yesterday. Please check the printed copy when you arrive and tell the desk immediately if anything has been missed.

Cheers,
Wes

For the next visit we have noted:
- wipe the high shelves;
- vacuum beneath the display table;
- clean the fingerprints from the glass doors;
- replace the liners in the small bins.

Please tell us if the display will move before then so we can plan the order of the work.

Yori, we have moved the lunch area a little farther from the main path. That should make it easier for people to queue without blocking visitors who are walking through. The vehicle space is level and we will have someone there to guide you into position.

Please check these details:
- service starts at noon and finishes at two;
- the menu board goes at the start of the queue;
- the collection point is on the other side of the window;
- rubbish bins will be beside the picnic tables.

We will provide the queue markers and tables. Please bring your own signs for the food options. There is a covered area for people to eat if it rains, but it is a short walk from the vehicle, so lidded containers would help. We have asked the musicians to finish their sound check before you start serving. If you need to move the vehicle after the event, please wait until the crowd has cleared and speak to the steward first. Let me know if anything here differs from what you expected.

Nave
